            "sort": 1,
            "name": "Introduction",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"KDygdzHXmoLYnqxeNBSlhbHrg4c\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-GWpEd65Kvo67irx1kTvlpG7egfe\">Opinions are divided on whether museums should primarily serve educational purposes or focus on providing entertainment value. <strong>I think that it is no longer relevant for museums to exclusively focus on education in today&rsquo;s society, and the introduction of leisure and amusement aspects would be preferable.</strong></div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 12868,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 78,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"KDygdzHXmoLYnqxeNBSlhbHrg4c\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Q0bzd9iaao54RbxaiL0lxfXmgYs\"><strong>Proponents of education as a primary motivation for how museums should operate could present some valid arguments. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(45, 194, 107);\">They argue that the main purpose of these facilities is to cater to those seeking tangible learning opportunities and practical experiences beyond traditional sources of knowledge. For example, science museums allow visitors to engage with detailed dinosaur models and sense the prehistoric world first-hand, thereby gaining a deeper understanding of natural history - an experience that written documents alone can hardly live up to. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(53, 152, 219);\">Nevertheless, although I acknowledge the educational value that this approach can bring about, I am convinced that relying solely on static displays and written information is rather boring and tedious. This could ultimately lead to a decline in visitor counts and affect a museum&rsquo;s operations in the long run.</span></div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 12868,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 79,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"KDygdzHXmoLYnqxeNBSlhbHrg4c\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-DtwQdu5LNoDR0Zxf6zzltxG6gLh\"><strong>Therefore, I believe that it is advisable for museums to incorporate elements of entertainment to provide maximum value to visitors and adapt to modern expectations. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(45, 194, 107);\">By offering recreational services and enjoyable experiences, museums can create an inviting atmosphere that encourages people of all ages to come and explore. As a result, increased visitor engagement generates more financial resources for the preservation of precious objects, helping maintain their accessibility to the public. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(53, 152, 219);\">Furthermore, becoming more entertainment-oriented can turn museums into an environment more conducive to knowledge acquisition. For example, amenities like interactive games, virtual reality experiences or theatrical performances can simplify complex concepts and make exhibits more engaging to young visitors, fostering a sense of curiosity and encouraging them to actively learn more about the subject matter.</span></div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 12868,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 80,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Conclusion",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"KDygdzHXmoLYnqxeNBSlhbHrg4c\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-IcMLdzinToLpatx6uWXlm5KBgmb\">In conclusion, while prioritizing educational value is crucial for museums to fulfill their mission of preserving and disseminating knowledge, I firmly believe that integrating entertainment elements is essential to ensure their sustainability and relevance in the modern world.</div>\n</div>",
